Then run gradle with -I to print classpath for :ji-remote-bootstrap.

Let me create the files with apply_patch.

First, the init script:

```groovy
allprojects { p ->
    p.tasks.register('printRuntimeCp') {
        doLast {
            def ss = p.extensions.findByName('sourceSets')
            if (ss != null) {
                println "JI_CP=" + p.files(ss.getByName('main').runtimeClasspath).asPath
            }
        }
    }
}
```
Note: with configuration cache this may complain; add `--no-configuration-cache`.

Then compile: `javac -cp <cp> -d attachments/repro/classes attachments/repro/RaceRepro.java` and run `java -cp <cp>;classes RaceRepro`.

The repro program:

```java
import io.github.diodeme.ji.remote.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.time.Duration;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public final class RaceRepro {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Path dataDir = Files.createTempDirectory("ji-orch-repro-");
        List<Map<String,String>> events = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
        CountDownLatch scanStarted = new CountDownLatch(1);
        CountDownLatch release = new CountDownLatch(1);
        String scanned = "deploy-alias ssh-ed25519 " + Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString("blob".getBytes());

        ProcessRunner runner = new ProcessRunner() {
            @Override public ProcessRunner.Result run(List<String> command, Duration timeout) {
                if (command.getFirst().equals("ssh-keyscan")) {
                    scanStarted.countDown();
                    try { release.await(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS); } catch (InterruptedException e) { Thread.currentThread().interrupt(); }
                    return new ProcessRunner.Result(0, scanned + "\n", "");
                }
                return new ProcessRunner.Result(0, "", "");
            }
            @Override public ProcessRunner.RunningProcess start(List<String> command) {
                return new ProcessRunner.RunningProcess() {
                    @Override public boolean isAlive() { return true; }
                    @Override public void close() {}
                };
            }
        };
        ...
    }
}
```

I need the exact signatures of ProcessRunner (Result, RunningProcess) — it was modified in this round (+10 lines). Let me check ProcessRunner.java.

Also RemoteOrchestration constructor: `public RemoteOrchestration(ProcessRunner processes, SshKnownHosts knownHosts, OrchestrationAudit audit)`.

And `submit(new Request(commandId, Action.CONNECT, new Target(host, Optional.empty(), OptionalInt.empty(), Optional.empty(), false), Optional.empty()))`.

Wait, Request takes Target record with (host, user Optional<String>, port OptionalInt, identityFile Optional<Path>, allowPrivateAddresses). And the policy validates host (must not be private by default; "deploy-alias" unresolvable → allowed).

SshKnownHosts.inDataDirectory(dir) exists.

Then:
- submit → operation starts worker → runner.run("ssh-keyscan") blocks → after scanStarted, call cancel(id) → returns cancelled. events should have 1.
- then release latch → worker proceeds → await → state reset → OperationCancelledException → terminate → second audit.
- wait for the worker to finish: poll until events.size() >= 2 or timeout.
- print result.

